invariant: INV-14
file: handshake_parser_ee.c
catches: handshake_strict_webpki
reason: the parser admits an empty server_name acknowledgement whether
  or not the ClientHello sent server_name. A pins-only configuration
  without a hostname sends none, and RFC 6066 §3 gives the server
  nothing to acknowledge there, so RFC 9846 §4.3 makes the reply an
  unrequested extension: unsupported_extension.
  bin/handshake_strict_webpki's not-sent row objects.

--- old
    if (ext == EXT_SERVER_NAME && out->server_name_sent) {
--- new
    if (ext == EXT_SERVER_NAME) {
